  title One telnet keystroke on the wire: 41 bytes, 40 are header
  desc The fixed per-packet cost (40-byte TCP/IP header) dwarfs the 1-byte payload — 97.5% overhead, the arithmetic that motivated Nagle and every batcher since
  values
    - label TCP/IP header (fixed cost)
      value 40
    - label Payload (variable)
      value 1
